Task: Replace Custom Limit Name MultiSelect with ICGDS MultiSelect Component

I want to replace the existing custom multi-select dropdown implementation in the Limit Summary screen with the standard ICGDS Select component, using its Multiple Mode functionality.

I have two reference implementations:

1. ICGDS Multiple Mode: The existing standard component demonstrated in the ICGDS component documentation.
2. Current Limit Summary implementation: The existing custom dropdown with search functionality, checkboxes, an ALL option, and multi-selection.

Use the existing ICGDS component implementation as the reference and migrate the Limit Name filter to use it.

1. First, analyze the existing implementation

Before making any changes:

* Locate the Limit Summary component.
* Identify the existing Limit Name dropdown implementation.
* Understand how the current search functionality works.
* Identify how selected values are maintained in state.
* Identify how the ALL selection works.
* Check how selected values trigger API calls or grid filtering.
* Identify any existing CSS or custom logic associated with this dropdown.
* Inspect the ICGDS Select component documentation and actual implementation.

ICGDS documentation reference:
/icgds/react/components/select/overview#SimpleMultiSelectMode

Check the actual component props, supported features, styling capabilities, and event handlers before implementing.

Do not assume unsupported props or introduce another third-party library.

2. Replace with ICGDS Multiple Mode

Use the standard ICGDS Select component with its Multiple Mode.

Expected functionality:

* Multiple values should be selectable.
* Each option should have a checkbox.
* Search functionality should be available.
* Existing selected values should be retained when opening the dropdown.
* Support clearing selected values.
* Preserve the existing Limit Summary filtering and API integration.

Use the actual supported ICGDS properties, following its documentation. The implementation may use properties such as:

* mode=“multiple”
* placeholder
* allowClear
* autoCollapseTags
* highlightOption
* defaultValue / value
* onChange

Verify the exact API and controlled/uncontrolled behavior before using them.

3. Configurable selected-value display (Important)

I want the flexibility to decide whether selected values are displayed as tags or not.

Implement a configurable property:

showSelectedAsTags

Expected behavior:

When showSelectedAsTags = true:

* Display selected values as tags inside the Select input.
* Avoid excessive expansion when multiple values are selected.
* Use the ICGDS auto-collapse functionality if supported.

When showSelectedAsTags = false:

* Do not display individual selected-value tags.
* Keep the dropdown input compact.
* Display a suitable placeholder or selected count if supported by the component.
* The selected checkboxes must still remain checked when reopening the dropdown.
* Do not lose selected values from the internal state.

Make this configurable rather than hardcoding either behavior.

4. Configurable ALL option (Important)

The current implementation has an ALL checkbox.

I want a configurable property:

showAllOption

Expected behavior:

* When true, display ALL as the first option in the dropdown.
* When false, do not display ALL in the dropdown.
* ALL should not be treated as a normal Limit Name value.
* Selecting ALL should select all available Limit Names.
* Deselecting ALL should clear the selection.
* If all individual values are selected manually, handle the ALL checkbox state appropriately.
* When searching, ALL should remain a separate control and should not be treated as a regular search result.
* Verify that selecting and deselecting individual options works correctly after using ALL.

